        {
          "label": "Suggested Correction",
          "value": "Add note OR replace Mereka with Munach (עַמּוּדֵיהֶ֣ם)."
        },
        {
          "label": "Critical Note",
          "value": "Going by appearance, this mark does not look like a Mereka due to its slant. Dotan has a Munach. This word is in the domain of Zaqef Qatan, and the servant of Zaqef Qatan is always Munach. Price noted BHS and BHK erroneously have Mereka, which is possibly a defect in L (Page 65, Syntax of Masoretic Accents)."
        }
      ],
